  "title": "Refused: a process role is not a conserved component (CG-08)",
  "description": "This graph contains the two most tempting component edges in the whole repository, and the two the audit says must not be drawn.\n\nZielinski's StreamKind vocabulary (wet_biomass, inclusion_bodies, chromatographic_fraction, ...) names process ROLES, not chemical species: an inclusion body is not a substance. No Zielinski stream carries a component amount or a mass fraction at all, and none of the twenty registered equations produces one.\n\nEdge 1 and edge 2 supply a Morris control volume from such a port. Both are refused: the source names no component, so it cannot be assigned to zinc or to copper, and the boundary would in any case be one Chapter 4 cannot represent.\n\nEdge 3 supplies copper where zinc is expected. Both sides declare their components perfectly well; they simply disagree. That is refused too, because connecting them would relabel the substance -- the failure mode that turns a copper charge into an inclusion-body charge without anything looking wrong.",
  "source_ref": "Zielinski et al. (2019) sec. 4.2 and 4.3; Morris et al. (2011), Chapter 4",
  "notes": "Expected: connection.component_unattributed on edges 1 and 2, connection.component_mismatch on edge 3, plus capability.reactive_balance_refused on the two edges that cross the Zielinski boundary.",
